\section*{Conformal nets and representation equivalence for strongly rational unitary VOAs}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. Simple strongly rational unitary VOAs are claimed to generate completely rational nets, with unitary modules and a braided unitary equivalence to finite-index sectors.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} Take a vertex operator algebra \(V\) over \(\mathbb C\); require simplicity, unitarity and strong rationality. Then the source claims polynomial energy bounds and strong locality of the smeared fields, producing an irreducible conformal net \(A_V\). It also asserts complete unitarity of \(V\), strong integrability for unitary grading-restricted finite-length modules, and complete rationality of \(A_V\). With invariant positive Hermitian forms on simple modules, the representation categories are claimed to obey
\[
 \operatorname{Rep}(V)\simeq\operatorname{Rep}^{u}(V)
 \xrightarrow{F_{\mathrm{CWX}}^{V}}\operatorname{Rep}^{f}(A_V),
\]
a braided unitary tensor equivalence. The net category uses Connes fusion and DHR braiding with matching circle orientation. Strong rationality here includes simplicity, CFT type, self-contragredience, rationality, and \(C_2\)-cofiniteness; the source does not extend this theorem to every unitary VOA.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Energy bounds establish strong locality of the generating fields. Annular charged-field estimates integrate modules, positive fusion forms give unitary tensor structure, and rationality identifies net sectors; the cited extension theorems then relate local net extensions to conformal VOA extensions.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Simple strongly rational unitary VOAs are claimed to generate completely rational nets, with unitary modules and a braided unitary equivalence to finite-index sectors. The question retains these same parameters and conventions. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 280, the documented entry establishes energy bounds, strong locality, and an irreducible conformal-net construction. Complete rationality, unitary module classification, tensor equivalence, and extension classification are omitted. The listed Comparator files are \texttt{VertexAlgebraNet.lean}. The inventory does not supply a named declaration for these Comparator entries. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

